(N'雨碎江南', N'9', N'youtube', N'No one reads these after 8 years but this makes me understand the meaning of the word &quot;hiraeth&quot;: a Welsh word that describes a deep, nostalgic longing for a home to which you cannot return, or a home that may never have existed. It&#39;s a complex feeling encompassing homesickness, but with a deeper, more profound sense of yearning for something lost or unattainable, even if that &quot;something&quot; is a place, time, or person that never truly existed. <br>It moves me towards a place that is not there.', N'117', N'2024-05-24'),
